IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-art9-restricted-section`
IMPORT `g3-art10-public-access`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT to fail.  Each is an expectation a careful reader might bring to the Articles -- the survey's own expectation, a purposive
-- reading, the other reading of a fork run against the favoured one -- written as an assertion and run against the encoding.  Every one fails, and the number is fixed:
-- TWELVE failed assertions, no refused one.  check.sh lists this file in expected_failed with that count, and FRAGMENT-G3.md says why each fails.
-- Beside proving that the harness can fail, the file records where the favoured reading departs from a natural expectation.

§ `Expectations that the favoured readings do not meet`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

`the 2019 constitution` MEANS
    `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH
        kind IS `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it`
        `date received or made` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date it ceased to be operative` IS NOTHING

`general then restricted before deregistration` MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` WITH
        `placements of the entity before deregistration` IS LIST (`a placement in` `the general section` `on` (YMD 2019 3 1)), (`a placement in` `the restricted section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1))
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `matters prescribed by an Order under Article 8(5)(e)` IS EMPTY

`restricted before deregistration` MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` WITH
        `placements of the entity before deregistration` IS LIST (`a placement in` `the restricted section` `on` (YMD 2019 3 1))
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `matters prescribed by an Order under Article 8(5)(e)` IS EMPTY

`a 30 June year-end and a return for the year to 30 June 2026` MEANS
    `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH
        `a date on which the charity's financial year ends` IS JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)
        `annual returns sent` IS LIST (`Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH `last day of the year to which it relates` IS YMD 2026 6 30, `date sent` IS YMD 2026 9 1)

`the unincorporated body with a flat as its main premises` MEANS
    `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH
        `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS NOTHING
        `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS JUST (`Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))` WITH address IS "7 Elm Close", `in Jersey` IS TRUE, `a private dwelling house` IS TRUE, `at or from which the charity undertakes an activity` IS TRUE)
        `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS LIST "3 Rue Bas"

-- RED 1.  The survey's discriminating case for its reading C of F3.1 (PLAN section (g)): "a constitution copy received 2019-03-01 by a charity still registered; asked on 2029-03-02: may it be discarded?
-- A yes, B no, C yes".  Run against reading C as this encoding defines it (ten years from the day the copy ceases to be operative), the copy of a constitution that is still operative may NOT be discarded.
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `interpretation F3.1 reading C` `the 2019 constitution` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2029 3 2)

-- RED 2.  Purposive reading of Article 8(3)(a)(i) on sub-paragraph (ba) (F3.13): an NPO body corporate within (ba) ought to carry the "also within (a)" statement.  The text names (f) to (j) only; none is made.
#ASSERT (`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` fav (`an entity falling within` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`)))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- RED 3.  Likewise Article 8(3)(a)(ii): details of the Jersey law by which a (ba) body is established ought to be required, as for (e) and (g).  The text does not list (ba).
#ASSERT (`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` fav (`an entity falling within` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`)))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`

-- RED 4.  The other reading of F3.11 (any time in the general section counts) run against the favoured one: a charity entered in the general section, then in the restricted section, then deregistered,
-- is NOT one that "was registered in the general section" immediately before deregistration.
#ASSERT `Art 8(5)(b) the entity was registered in the general section` fav `general then restricted before deregistration`

-- RED 5.  The other reading of F3.3 run against the favoured one: a purported designation of a matter in the historic section does NOT make it non-public, because Article 10(4) reaches a registered charity only.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(3) the matter is in a public part of the register` fav `a company, formerly registered` (`an item required by Article 8(5)` `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`) TRUE

-- RED 6.  The literal reading of "the applicant" in Article 9(2) (F3.12 reading B) run against the favoured one: a charity in the general section that meets the funding condition CAN request.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(2) the request for entry in the restricted section may be made` fav `a company in the general section` TRUE FALSE

-- RED 7.  Article 9(1)(a) hides the registered name of a restricted-section charity.  The expectation that the name is one of the public elements is wrong.
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `the registered name`

-- RED 8.  A day edge: with the day of the event not counted, a copy received on 1 March 2019 may be discarded on 2 March 2029, not on the anniversary itself.
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` fav `the 2019 constitution` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2029 3 1)

-- RED 9.  A plain registered charity does not need all fourteen items: (d), (h), (i), (k), (l), (m) and (n) are conditional.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS `the fourteen items of Article 8(3)`

-- RED 10.  The survey's own illustration of F3.2: a charity with a 30 June year-end that filed for the year to 30 June 2026 is NOT one that has sent its annual return for the most recent year under the calendar-year reading,
-- on 1 February 2027 (the most recent calendar year is 2026).
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` (YMD 2027 2 1) `a 30 June year-end and a return for the year to 30 June 2026`

-- RED 11.  Where the main premises are a private dwelling house the Law would be thought to leave no principal address (F3.10 reading B).  The favoured reading falls back to the governors' addresses.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav (`an entity falling within` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`)) `the unincorporated body with a flat as its main premises` EQUALS EMPTY

-- RED 12.  A charity that was in the restricted section has its former name entered in the historic section (compare Article 9(1)(a) for the live register).  Article 8(5)(b) enters no name for it.
#ASSERT `Art 8(5)(b) the names to be entered in the historic section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` `restricted before deregistration` EQUALS LIST "Alpha Charity Limited"
